WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.027 --> 00:00:02.000
(upbeat music)
- What's up guys, I'm K.J.,

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.040
I'm here at BuzzFeed and I'm
gonna be cuddling some puppies

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.590
while I answer some fan questions,

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.650
and I can't wait, give
me the pups, let's go!

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:11.233
(upbeat music)

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.927
(lips smacking)

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.340
(exclaims)

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:32.286
Okay!
(upbeat music)

00:00:32.286 --> 00:00:34.820
I got that from being on a trampoline,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.580
I was four years old and
I cracked my head open

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.670
on the side of the trampoline.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.553
And I almost died, near death experience.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.198
Girlfriend, and burger.

00:00:48.198 --> 00:00:49.600
Those are the hardest ones.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.600
These are my kids, they're like my kids!

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:55.503
Some of my favorite actors,

00:00:55.503 --> 00:00:58.462
I really enjoy Ricky Gervais,
I think he's really funny.

00:00:58.462 --> 00:01:01.300
I really like, who else do I like?

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.670
Vince Vaughn, I like funny guys,

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.464
I like watching funny actors.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:08.500
Music, Van Halen, Led
Zeppelin, I love everything,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.800
I love all kinds of music.

00:01:14.613 --> 00:01:16.460
Definitely never gonna dye it again.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.420
Yeah I get it dyed every two weeks,

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.590
and it's like the roots, I
have to get all the roots

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:21.880
and stuff done every two weeks,

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.417
and yeah, I really hope that
I don't go bald when I'm 30.

00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:28.000
(upbeat music)

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:30.693
Probably not!

00:01:30.693 --> 00:01:32.950
I probably would have
been friends with Jug,

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.800
but I don't know if I would
have been friends with Archie.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.440
I think we would have been rivals maybe.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.360
We would have been both
on the football team,

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.810
we would have had a similar relationship

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.670
to Archie and Reggie,
you know what I mean,

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:42.870
like their relationship?

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.370
Pick one, just pick one
and see if it works out

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:52.053
before you try everyone in
the whole school! (laughing)

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.640
Interesting question
actually, because season five

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.560
we're kind of unsure on
what we're gonna be doing,

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:02.330
but I think it would be
cool if I was in the army

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.137
or something and I came back
and I was like you know,

00:02:04.137 --> 00:02:06.490
and I didn't go to college
and I went into the army

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:07.640
or something, that would be cool.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:08.550
We could shoot me like

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:11.743
Archie's like in the
war, you know! (laughing)

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.680
I want Archie to be single,
focus on him for a second

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.640
instead of why does he always
have to be with someone?

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.401
Maybe he can just chill
and just focus on himself.

00:02:22.401 --> 00:02:24.010
Maybe he should get a dog?

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.933
Maybe he should get a
little puppy? (laughing)

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:35.030
I think the idea of Archie
and Betty is really cool,

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:38.400
just because it's so iconic
and I think the whole endgame

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.820
like Archie and Betty being endgames

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:40.780
is something really cool

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.067
I think the fans would really love that.

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:43.960
You're just gonna climb all over me!

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.190
With saying what I just said,

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.240
I would probably say Bughead,
I really like Bughead,

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.236
I think fans love Bughead.

00:02:49.236 --> 00:02:50.730
You know, I think right now

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.968
it's exactly where it needs to be.

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:54.266
I wish I was a dog!

00:02:54.266 --> 00:02:56.004
Just no worries in the world.

00:02:56.004 --> 00:02:57.178
Look at him!

00:02:57.178 --> 00:02:58.563
He looks like a chipmunk.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.730
No, we don't have any on-set rituals.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.790
We just kind of hang
out before we go on set,

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.060
and it's honestly it's not that often

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.560
we all get to work with each other,

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.160
when we're all in the same scene

00:03:11.208 --> 00:03:12.280
it's kind of a, it's really fun

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.033
but it's not often when that happens.

00:03:16.621 --> 00:03:18.833
I'd say Cole and Charles, yeah.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.220
At this point no, I haven't
heard anything about that,

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.053
that would be really cool though,

00:03:25.053 --> 00:03:27.193
I'd love to go to New York
and shoot with those guys.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.800
I don't know, I think Cole's
pretty similar to Jughead,

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.490
just the broody kind-of, you
know he's intelligent too,

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:36.600
he's pretty funny, he's
got a dark sense of humor.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.910
Sorry bro, I know he would hate
to hear that, but it's true.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:40.800
We're all pretty similar
to our characters, I think.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.640
You know and I think in a way
that's why actors get cast,

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.480
because they bring their
energy to the character

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.490
as well as bringing everything
else that the writing gives,

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:51.640
But Nathalie Boltt who
plays Penelope Blossom

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:52.810
is a really incredible actor

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:55.030
because she plays the weirdness
of that character so well,

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:56.310
I think she's probably the most different

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.043
because she's a really
incredible person in real life.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.760
When I'm not filming I get
into it even more actually,

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.593
because I have more time,

00:04:05.593 --> 00:04:07.430
it's harder actually when I'm not.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.870
When I'm working, just
'cause of the amount of time

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.076
that we have to shoot and stuff.

00:04:12.076 --> 00:04:13.203
(dog whimpering)
Oh!

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:18.650
I work out with a guy called Alex Fine.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.640
Me and Charles, Charles
introduced me to him.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:21.980
When I work out with him I stay with him,

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.320
usually over a weekend,

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.580
and he kind of gets me into the rhythm,

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:25.830
so that I can go back to Vancouver

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.020
and keep everything up again.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.300
It's harder, you gotta cycle it,

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.170
you have three weeks on

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.006
where you're working out really hard,

00:04:32.006 --> 00:04:33.229
and then you gotta take a week off

00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:35.022
'cause you can't sustain working that much

00:04:35.022 --> 00:04:37.741
and then working out on
top of that too, you know?

00:04:37.741 --> 00:04:41.610
These puppies were provided
by Vanderpump Dogs.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:42.830
If you want more information

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:45.141
you can visit vanderpumpdogs.org

00:04:45.141 --> 00:04:50.141
(upbeat music)
(dogs whimpering)

